; CPF merge for the CODE instance of stack 2 - the instance that owns the code,
; classes and utilities.
;
; Prepared here:
;   - SuperUser is logon-ready
;   - TRAINCODE database exists: this stays local and holds the classes and
;     routines for the whole exercise
;   - TRAINING namespace exists with BOTH its routines and its globals pointing at
;     the local TRAINCODE database
;
; The starting state is deliberately "everything local". The exercise moves only
; the globals (the data) onto the DATA instance over ECP, leaving the routines
; local - which is exactly the target architecture: code and utilities on this
; instance, the data they operate on somewhere else.
;
; Deliberately NOT prepared - this is the exercise (see ../EXERCISE.md):
;   - no ECP server definition pointing at the data instance
;   - no remote database
;   - TRAINING globals are still local

[Actions]
ModifyUser:Name=SuperUser,ChangePassword=0

CreateDatabase:Name=TRAINCODE,Directory=/usr/irissys/mgr/traincode

CreateNamespace:Name=TRAINING,Globals=TRAINCODE,Routines=TRAINCODE
